From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] uiautomationcore: pattern objects of the COM client, pattern properties

IUIAutomationElement::GetCurrentPattern and GetCurrentPatternAs returned E_NOTIMPL, so a
client could not drive any pattern through the COM API.

 - The element gives an object for the Invoke, ExpandCollapse, Toggle, Value, RangeValue,
   SelectionItem, ScrollItem, Scroll, Dock, Transform, Window, VirtualizedItem, MultipleView,
   SynchronizedInput and LegacyIAccessible patterns: every action goes to the provider and
   its error is the result, the Current properties come from the property values and the
   Cached ones from the cache request (E_INVALIDARG when not fetched).
 - A pattern the element does not support is S_OK with no object; asking for another
   interface than the pattern's is E_NOINTERFACE; a pattern without a client object yet is
   E_NOTIMPL.
 - The properties of those patterns (toggle state, value, range, scroll, window, ...) had no type
   information, so UiaGetPropertyValue answered E_NOTIMPL for them; they now come from the
   pattern provider, as the properties that already did (Value.IsReadOnly, LegacyIAccessible role).
